                "summary": "Position: don't add a mechanical dissent/agreement gate to panel.mjs yet. (1) The spec already decided agreement is passive measurement, not a gate, with pre-committed K2/K3/K5 review conditions (runner.md:1435) and agreement/genuineSplit metrics (observe.md:61). (2) The council mechanisms already exist as Workflow steps: anonymizeInputs (runner.md:1437), blind (runner.md:1439), independent panelists (panel.mjs:63-68), and a synthesizer on a different provider (panel.mjs:94-97). A gate would add hidden sequencing that ADR 0047 avoided (runner.md:3050). (3) Red-team doesn't cover panels (reviewed.mjs:27-28,52-54), and the panel outcome is just the synthesizer's outcome (panel.mjs:101-104), so the real gap is showing splits to the owner, not forcing dissent. I would change my mind if K2/K3 fires or if panels run single-provider in practice (runner.md:1404-1405). Next step: collect stance data on 30 panel runs and check K2/K3 with fgos metrics discussions; meanwhile pass the measured genuineSplit into the panel result (read-only, non-gating).",
